## Hedonism-First Identity

The intended perfume is a red-gold floral light falling onto black suede, then melting into warm skin. Bergamot supplies polish; red mandarin supplies pleasure and color; pink pepper turns citrus sparkle into rose tension. Rose de Mai gives the recognizable flower, Osmanthus gives a naturally leather-adjacent apricot shadow, AIMI makes the flower tactile rather than bouquet-like, and Suederal supplies the dark object. The finish should be soft, intimate, and addictive rather than dry, loud, or gourmand.

Four perceptual modules own the perfume:

| Module | Owners | Hedonic job | Rejection signal |
|---|---|---|---|
| red-gold invitation | Bergamot, Red Mandarin, Pink Pepper, Safraleine | bright warmth and rosy spice without a busy citrus/spice catalogue | orange candy, shampoo, tobacco |
| luminous living flower | Hedione, Dihydrojasmone, Rose de Mai, Osmanthus, PEA, Alpha Damascone | recognizable rose light with apricot-leather curvature and movement | jam, peach perfume, soap, blank jasmine |
| powder-suede gravity | AIMI, Suederal, IBQ, Evernyl, vetiver, patchouli | bends the flower around a dark tactile center | lipstick, rubber, oakmoss, dirty patchouli |
| warm petal-skin trail | Iso E, cedar, Ambrox, Cashmeran, Ebanol, Ambrettolide, Hexyl Salicylate, Benzyl Benzoate, benzoin/vanillin | smooth persistent body and intimate sensuality | generic woody amber, fruity musk, sandal cream, vanilla |

The formula happens to use **26 aromatic materials plus DEP**. The count is a result of retained functions, not a complexity quota.

